1
00:00:03,401 --> 00:00:17,441
A laundry room for the Reyes family: a broom closet and cabinets over the washer and dryer.

2
00:00:17,441 --> 00:00:24,638
A 24" x 84" tall cabinet at the left end becomes the broom closet.

3
00:00:24,638 --> 00:00:36,719
Over the washer and dryer: a 36" and a 24" wall cabinet, 30" high.

4
00:00:36,719 --> 00:00:47,766
The wall is 84": 24" for the closet, 60" for the side-by-side washer and dryer.

5
00:00:47,766 --> 00:00:55,093
Arrange: the tall cabinet stands at the left; the wall cabinets hang at 54" beside it.

6
00:00:55,093 --> 00:00:57,697
The uppers top out at 84", level with the closet, leaving 54" for the machines below.

7
00:00:57,697 --> 00:01:05,369
Make the 24" one an open shelf for detergent: set its doors to None.

8
00:01:05,369 --> 00:01:20,461
W2 is now open: the elevation draws its two shelves and no doors, and so does the 3D.

9
00:01:20,461 --> 00:01:29,543
Cut list: the open cabinet has no doors and no hinges, so the hardware total drops too.

10
00:01:29,543 --> 00:01:33,897
Nesting: a small job on a few sheets, with offcuts kept for the next one.

11
00:01:33,897 --> 00:01:39,331
Labels and sheet maps are on the Output tab. Machine output switches stay off.

12
00:01:39,331 --> 00:01:42,334
A laundry room in a few minutes: one tall cabinet, two uppers, one of them open.
